    "introduction": "Land Securities, commonly known as Landsec, owns and develops commercial property in the UK. Its portfolio includes workplaces, retail destinations and development opportunities intended to create or improve urban locations. Revenue primarily comes from rent paid by occupiers, while development and asset management can change the value and earning potential of properties. The business must attract tenants, maintain buildings and decide where to invest or recycle capital. Results are influenced by occupancy, rental growth, property valuations and financing costs. Changes in office use and shopping patterns affect demand, making location, building quality and the long-term adaptability of its assets important.",
